// An enum has no agreed spelling in XML, so `#[derive(Xml)]` refuses one and says why rather
// than picking a convention for its caller. Reaching the generator's own message at all needed
// the enum half of the user-generator path in `src/derive.c`: before 2026-10-31 this reported
// "unknown derive target 'Xml'", which was the compiler answering a question it was not asked.
use xml

#[derive(Xml)]
enum Colour {
    Red
    Green
}

fn main() {
    print(1)
}
